From 6db59f768d8e555de6a11d37299e1b21c974ba8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 01:26:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] net: hix5hd2_gmac: hold the MAC core reset long enough

hix5hd2_mac_core_reset() asserts and immediately deasserts the MAC core
reset.  Both operations are a single read-modify-write of one CRG
register, so the reset is only held for the handful of cycles between
the two stores.

On the Hi3798MV200 that pulse is too short for the MAC to act on.  The
core comes up in an undefined state and its MDIO block never drives the
bus, so every management read returns all ones and no PHY is ever
discovered:

  mdio_bus f9840000.ethernet-mii: MDIO device at address 3 is missing.

Follow the reset sequence the vendor driver uses: start from a known
deasserted state, then hold the reset asserted for 50us before releasing
it again.  The extra 100us only happens once per probe.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
index 0665f1cd9da3..89ab8dfe128d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
@@ -1050,12 +1050,24 @@ static void hix5hd2_destroy_sg_desc_queue(struct hix5hd2_priv *priv)
 	}
 }
 
-static inline void hix5hd2_mac_core_reset(struct hix5hd2_priv *priv)
+static void hix5hd2_mac_core_reset(struct hix5hd2_priv *priv)
 {
 	if (!priv->mac_core_rst)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Start from a known deasserted state and hold the reset long
+	 * enough for it to take effect.  Asserting and deasserting back
+	 * to back only produces a pulse a few register writes wide, which
+	 * is too short for the MAC to act on, and leaves its MDIO block
+	 * wedged so that every read returns all ones.
+	 */
+	reset_control_deassert(priv->mac_core_rst);
+	usleep_range(50, 60);
+
 	reset_control_assert(priv->mac_core_rst);
+	usleep_range(50, 60);
+
 	reset_control_deassert(priv->mac_core_rst);
 }
 
